  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Sumatran Orangutan Populations and their Habitats in the Western Part of the Leuser Ecosystem, Aceh Province, Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Among the significant locations for orangutans in Aceh, three places stand out as important: Ketambe, Suaq Belimbing and Soraya. All three have good populations of orangutan and all have important Research Stations for the Leuser Ecosystem. Forum Konservasi Leuser (FKL) manages Ketambe and Soraya Research Stations, while Suaq Belimbing Station is managed by Yayasan Ekosistem Lestari. All three stations are threatened by encroachment, illegal logging and illegal hunting. FKL has established a protection system for these research stations and the surrounding forest area called the Community Patrol Team (CPT). CPTs conduct patrols to look for forest destruction and poachers, and also participate in forest restoration activities. The CPTs require USFWS support to enhance their training and expand their patrol and forest restoration activities. The objectives of this project are the following: (1) Training of Community Patrol Teams; (2) Equip and support Community Patrol Teams; (3) Community patrols and reduces illegal activity; and, (4) Forest restoration in orangutan habitat.</narrative>
  </description>
